49 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     When Amanda came home from her first day of school, she was confused. She stopped in the doorway with a puzzled look on her face and crossed her arms. Her dad, walking in the hallway, noticed Amanda\220s expression and paused.      \215What\220s the matter, sweetie?\216 he asked.  Amanda scratched her head. \215I met a lot of new classmates today at school, which I expected,\216 she said. \215But I didn\220t expect them to be so different from me.\216      \215What do you mean?\216)/E(     When Amanda came home from her first day of school, she was confused. She stopped in the doorway with a puzzled look on her face and crossed her arms. Her dad, walking in the hallway, noticed Amanda\220s expression and paused.      \215What\220s the matter, sweetie?\216 he asked.  Amanda scratched her head. \215I met a lot of new classmates today at school, which I expected,\216 she said. \215But I didn\220t expect them to be so different from me.\216      \215What do you mean?\216)/Alt()/Pg 9 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

50 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 28 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

51 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     Amanda recalled how her first day of school had gone. She was starting at a new school, so she had been excited to meet all of her new classmates. She yearned to make a best friend that was just like her.)/E(     Amanda recalled how her first day of school had gone. She was starting at a new school, so she had been excited to meet all of her new classmates. She yearned to make a best friend that was just like her.)/Alt()/Pg 10 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

52 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     That morning, she wore her favourite headband in her brown frizzy hair. She picked out her best outfit. She practised her smile in the mirror. She liked the way her eyes \205 one brown, one green \205 crinkled when she smiled.)/E(     That morning, she wore her favourite headband in her brown frizzy hair. She picked out her best outfit. She practised her smile in the mirror. She liked the way her eyes \205 one brown, one green \205 crinkled when she smiled.)/Alt()/Pg 10 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

53 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 29 0 R/Pg 11 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

54 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     Amanda walked into her new classroom with her backpack and a big smile, ready to greet her new classmates. But when she took a closer look around the room, she hesitated.      She saw people with black hair and blonde hair, people with blue eyes and brown eyes, people with pale skin and dark skin, tall people and short people... But she couldn\220t find anyone that looked just like her!)/E(     Amanda walked into her new classroom with her backpack and a big smile, ready to greet her new classmates. But when she took a closer look around the room, she hesitated.      She saw people with black hair and blonde hair, people with blue eyes and brown eyes, people with pale skin and dark skin, tall people and short people... But she couldn\220t find anyone that looked just like her!)/Alt()/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

55 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 30 0 R/Pg 12 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

56 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     \215Dad, I\220m confused,\216 said Amanda. \215Why doesn\220t anyone look like me? Is there something wrong with me?\216      Amanda\220s dad took her to the couch and sat her down. \215Not at all,\216 he reassured her. \215Everybody looks different because everybody is built uniquely.\216      \215What do you mean?\216)/E(     \215Dad, I\220m confused,\216 said Amanda. \215Why doesn\220t anyone look like me? Is there something wrong with me?\216      Amanda\220s dad took her to the couch and sat her down. \215Not at all,\216 he reassured her. \215Everybody looks different because everybody is built uniquely.\216      \215What do you mean?\216)/Alt()/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

57 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 31 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

58 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     Amanda\220s dad rubbed his hands together excitedly. He was a science teacher, and he absolutely adored giving scientific explanations to his daughter.      \215Deep, deep, inside of us is something called DNA. DNA determines how we look on the outside,\216 he explained. \215Some parts of it are different for everyone. We all look different because we all have different little parts.\216)/E(     Amanda\220s dad rubbed his hands together excitedly. He was a science teacher, and he absolutely adored giving scientific explanations to his daughter.      \215Deep, deep, inside of us is something called DNA. DNA determines how we look on the outside,\216 he explained. \215Some parts of it are different for everyone. We all look different because we all have different little parts.\216)/Alt()/Pg 13 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

59 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     \215So you have blonde hair, and I have brown hair, because we have different parts of DNA?\216 asked Amanda.       \215Exactly!\216 Her dad gave her a nod of encouragement.)/E(     \215So you have blonde hair, and I have brown hair, because we have different parts of DNA?\216 asked Amanda.       \215Exactly!\216 Her dad gave her a nod of encouragement.)/Alt()/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

60 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 32 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

61 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     Amanda took a moment to think about what her father had just explained to her. Amanda\220s hair was brown and frizzy because of her DNA. On the other hand, some of her dad\220s DNA was different, so his hair was blonde instead. Another question came to her mind.      \215Why do Mom and I have brown hair, but you have blonde hair?\216 she asked her dad.      \215Good question,\216 he said. \215Your traits are passed down from your parents. So even though I have blonde hair, Mom has brown hair. You get your brown hair from your mom, not me.\216)/E(     Amanda took a moment to think about what her father had just explained to her. Amanda\220s hair was brown and frizzy because of her DNA. On the other hand, some of her dad\220s DNA was different, so his hair was blonde instead. Another question came to her mind.      \215Why do Mom and I have brown hair, but you have blonde hair?\216 she asked her dad.      \215Good question,\216 he said. \215Your traits are passed down from your parents. So even though I have blonde hair, Mom has brown hair. You get your brown hair from your mom, not me.\216)/Alt()/Pg 14 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

62 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 33 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

63 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     \215There\220s a girl at school that has green streaks in her hair,\216 Amanda mused. \215Does that mean her mom has green hair, too?\216      Amanda\220s dad laughed. \215Not exactly. She wasn\220t born with green hair, so it\220s not a trait she got from her parents,\216 he explained. \215It\220s likely that she just used hair dye to turn it green.\216      \215I understand now,\216 replied Amanda. \215Thanks, Dad!\216)/E(     \215There\220s a girl at school that has green streaks in her hair,\216 Amanda mused. \215Does that mean her mom has green hair, too?\216      Amanda\220s dad laughed. \215Not exactly. She wasn\220t born with green hair, so it\220s not a trait she got from her parents,\216 he explained. \215It\220s likely that she just used hair dye to turn it green.\216      \215I understand now,\216 replied Amanda. \215Thanks, Dad!\216)/Alt()/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

64 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 34 0 R/Pg 16 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

65 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     Later that evening, Amanda was sitting at the dinner table with her parents. Dinner had just been served, and it looked delicious. But she was still too preoccupied to eat.      \215What\220s on your mind, Amanda?\216 her mom inquired.      \215Well, I understand that we\220re all unique because we have different DNA, but...\216 Amanda sighed. \215I\220m a little bummed that I\220ll never be able to make a best friend that\220s just like me.\216)/E(     Later that evening, Amanda was sitting at the dinner table with her parents. Dinner had just been served, and it looked delicious. But she was still too preoccupied to eat.      \215What\220s on your mind, Amanda?\216 her mom inquired.      \215Well, I understand that we\220re all unique because we have different DNA, but...\216 Amanda sighed. \215I\220m a little bummed that I\220ll never be able to make a best friend that\220s just like me.\216)/Alt()/Pg 16 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

66 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 35 0 R/Pg 17 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

67 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     Her dad let out a chuckle. \215Amanda, did you know that the DNA between any two humans is mostly identical? Only a tiny bit of your DNA is actually different!\216      Amanda\220s eyes lit up. \215Really? So I\220m not so different after all?\216      \215Exactly,\216 her mom chimed in. \215And anyway, you and your friend might have more in common than just outward appearances.\216      Amanda pondered her parents\220 words. Feeling inspired, she decided she would try something new the next day at school.)/E(     Her dad let out a chuckle. \215Amanda, did you know that the DNA between any two humans is mostly identical? Only a tiny bit of your DNA is actually different!\216      Amanda\220s eyes lit up. \215Really? So I\220m not so different after all?\216      \215Exactly,\216 her mom chimed in. \215And anyway, you and your friend might have more in common than just outward appearances.\216      Amanda pondered her parents\220 words. Feeling inspired, she decided she would try something new the next day at school.)/Alt()/Pg 17 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

68 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 36 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

69 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(     The next morning, Amanda marched into her classroom with purpose. She thought about everything she had learned the previous night about DNA and human differences.  Even though nobody else in this classroom looked exactly like her, she was okay with it. She knew that she could still make a new best friend.)/E(     The next morning, Amanda marched into her classroom with purpose. She thought about everything she had learned the previous night about DNA and human differences.  Even though nobody else in this classroom looked exactly like her, she was okay with it. She knew that she could still make a new best friend.)/Alt()/Pg 18 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

